  "id": "Compound::DB01016 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "The integrated evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Glyburide interacts with Cyp2c9, primarily through its classification as a sulfonylurea antidiabetic agent. Glyburide, along with other sulfonylureas like Glimepiride and Chlorpropamide, binds to Cyp2c9, indicating a shared pharmacological interaction. This binding is supported by the presence of a common lowest common ancestor in the glyburide-sulfonylurea pathway, reinforcing the notion of a conserved interaction across different sulfonylurea compounds. The consistent association across multiple paths highlights a plausible mechanism involving the inhibition of Cyp2c9, which is critical for drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Glyburide may modulate Cyp2c9 activity, potentially affecting the metabolism of other substrates. While the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated, the shared pathway and binding evidence provide a robust foundation for further investigation into the role of Cyp2c9 in glyburide metabolism.",
